 "notes": [
  "This set builds separate models, so the 6 groups are correct and I kept them. The booklet shows three models on separate pages: the workshop desk (pages 4-10), the arched stand (pages 11-21) and Aira's wing jetpack (pages 22-24). The step stool (page 10, step 13) is built on its own and only placed beside the desk, so it is a fourth group. The tan map tile (b93) and the trans-purple round tile (b94) are held by the minifigure, so they are the fifth and sixth groups. The minifigure's parts are not in the parts list, so there is nothing to attach them to.",
  "Exact stud-by-stud stacking is partly inferred from the small isometric drawings. In particular I assumed the wall layout of the desk, which bricks the magenta 2x4 plate and the slopes and columns sit on, and what each arch, headlight brick and corner plate rests on.",
  "Pieces that attach sideways have rests_on [] and are recorded in other_joins: the jumper plates, clip plates and clip tiles on the brackets, the ruler tile, the letter tile and the scissors.",
  "The wings of the stand (b65-b72) are only joined through the carrot tops, which clip into the clip plates and push into the headlight brick side holes. The booklet shows them swinging open and shut.",
  "Step stool: tile b35 sits on the exposed studs of the 2x3 plate and tiles b36 and b37 sit on the 2x2 brick. The picture is ambiguous."
 ],
